            <ArticleTitle>Prosthetic arthroplasty of the distal radioulnar joint: historical perspective and 24-year follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.hcl.2012.08.024</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0749-0712(12)00120-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a report of the first prosthetic hemiarthroplasty and full arthroplasty, designed and implanted for the distal radioulnar joint in 1988. Two case reports are presented, with follow-up of 24 years. Experience and problems in the design of both a hemiarthroplasty and total prosthetic arthroplasty are described, in the hope that future developments may avoid past failures.</AbstractText>
